      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we first represent the four integers in the form given by the remainders when divided by 11. Let these integers be denoted by $x, y, z,$ and $w$. This gives us the following congruences:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx &\\equiv 2 \\pmod{11} \\\\\ny &\\equiv 4 \\pmod{11} \\\\\nz &\\equiv 6 \\pmod{11} \\\\\nw &\\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nAccording to the problem, the remainder when the sum of these integers is divided by $11$ is what we need to find. Hence, we write:\n\n\\[\nx + y + z + w\n\\]\n\nUsing the properties of congruences, we combine the congruences:\n\n\\[\n(x + y + z + w) \\equiv (2 + 4 + 6 + 8) \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nAdding the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\n2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\nx + y + z + w \\equiv 20 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the remainder when $20$ is divided by $11$:\n\n\\[\n20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\n20 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nSo, the remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by $11$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
